## ⭐ Easy way to remember

```text
                INDEX ACCESS       FRONT/BACK OPERATIONS

C++ vector          ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐              ⭐⭐
C++ list            ⭐                    ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
C++ deque           ⭐⭐⭐⭐               ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Java ArrayList      ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐              ⭐⭐
Java LinkedList     ⭐                    ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Java ArrayDeque     ❌                   ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Python list         ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐              ⭐⭐
Python deque        ⭐⭐                 ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
```

**One correction to your notes:** Java's `LinkedList` does allow efficient insertion/removal at the ends, but saying it allows efficient insertion/deletion **"anywhere"** needs a qualification. Finding an arbitrary index is O(n); insertion/removal is O(1) once you already have the relevant node/iterator. That's why `LinkedList` isn't automatically better than `ArrayList` for arbitrary-position operations.




